By the sine formula, 
$$
\frac{8 \text{ cm}}{\sin \angle BAD} = \frac{11 \text{ cm}}{\sin 117^\circ}
$$
$$
\sin \angle BAD = \frac{8 \sin 117^\circ}{11}
$$
$$
\angle BAD = 40.391^\circ \text{ or } 180^\circ - 40.391^\circ \text{ (rejected)}
$$

In $\triangle ACD$, by the sine formula, 
$$
\frac{9 \text{ cm}}{\sin \angle DCB} = \frac{6 \text{ cm}}{\sin 30^\circ}
$$
$$
\sin \angle DCB = \frac{9 \sin 30^\circ}{6}
$$
$$
\angle DCB = 48.590^\circ, \text{ cor. to } 5 \text{ sig. fig.}
$$
